diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..ce829b7 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,12 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+Active webhooks receive a JSON POST for each subscribed event on their board. The body contains the event `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `board`, `creator`, and `eventable` (the card or comment). Verify `X-Webhook-Signature` against the hex HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body using the webhook’s signing secret.
+
+Fizzy makes one attempt per event and webhook; it does not follow redirects or retry ambiguous requests. A timeout can mean the receiver processed the event but its response was lost. Receivers can deduplicate by the `Idempotency-Key` header (the delivery ID). Destinations must resolve to a public IP address.
+
+A 2xx response counts as success. After at least ten consecutive failures spanning at least one hour, Fizzy deactivates the webhook. A success or reactivation resets the streak. Delivery logs are retained for one week.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
